# shellcheck configuration for tests/, containers/ and scripts/.
#
# Everything not listed here is a hard failure in CI, including the checks that catch the bugs that
# actually bite in this pipeline: unquoted expansions (SC2086), `trap` bodies quoted so they expand at
# trap time rather than at definition time (SC2064), and misused test operators.
#
# The three disabled below are style opinions this repository declines, not defects:
#
#   SC2155  "declare and assign separately". Applies to `readonly X="$(cmd)"`, which loses cmd's exit
#           status. Every use here is a path or a version string under `set -e` where the command
#           cannot meaningfully fail, and splitting them would cost the `readonly`.
#   SC2016  "expressions don't expand in single quotes". Every hit is deliberate: messages that quote
#           a shell command or a Rust panic string containing backticks.
#   SC2012  ls | wc -l. Used in a test stub, on globs of our own generated filenames, which
#           assets/schema_tiles.json constrains to [A-Za-z0-9_.-].
disable=SC2155,SC2016,SC2012
